186:If the check fails, a notice says why, for example *"Attempt 1 didn't pass: it added an axiom (`shortcut`), and only you can add beliefs. Asking Claude to retry."*, and Claude gets the exact failure and tries again. A statement written below a card with a blank line in between does not belong to the card (section 7's binding rule); the notice then says *"it left a blank line between “…” and its Lean statement"*, and Claude is told to remove the blank line. After the last allowed attempt (`telelean.run.maxGateAttempts`, 3 per round) telelean stops it and tells you, for example *"Claude's attempts didn't pass the checks 3 times: … telelean reverted its working copy to “Statements frozen (round 1)”."*: the proposal then shows the last state that passed (often the formalisation without a proof), which you can still accept, answer with Feedback, or discard.

